[0.064, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 65 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m**Why.** A script sees the world only through the events it is given and an option's inputs: enough    \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 66 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mfor a handler that reacts, not for one that looks around. Reload is what a modder needs to write       \r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m7\u001b[11G\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mscripts quickly. \u001b[29G    \u001b[34G   \u001b[38G     \u001b[44G    \u001b[49G       \u001b[57G   \u001b[61G      \u001b[68G  \u001b[71G  \u001b[74G     \u001b[80G   \u001b[84G  \u001b[87G        \u001b[96G       \u001b[104G      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 65 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m**Why.** A tree's task is where an NPC's script would act, and reload is what a modder needs to        \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 66 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mwrite scripts quickly.                                                                                 \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 67 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 68 \u001b[22m **What exists.** WAMR's interpreter, bounded by fuel and by a wall-time\u001b[K\r\u001b[7C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m9\u001b[11G\u001b[22m[\u001b[38;2;230;219;116mwatchdog\u001b[39m](glossary.md#watchdog)\u001b[44G(`script/ScriptHost.h`).\u001b[69GA\u001b[71Gscript\u001b[78Gis\u001b[81Ggranted\u001b[89G`log`,\u001b[96G`store`\u001b[104Gand\u001b[108Gone\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRan \u001b[1m7\u001b[22m shell commands · \u001b[38;2;255;107;128m1 failed\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mThe build, suites, tidy and links\u001b[37Gare\u001b[41Gall\u001b[45Gclean.\u001b[52GI'm\u001b[56Gfixing\u001b[63Gthe\u001b[67Gblank\u001b[73Glines\u001b[79Gin\u001b[82G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mScriptHost.cpp\u001b[97G\u001b[39mand\u001b[101Gcommitting\u001b[112Gpart\u001b[117G2.\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mMade \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m scratchpad edit \u001b[38;2;56;166;96m+16\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m, committed \u001b[1m8625139\u001b[22m, ran \u001b[1m4\u001b[22m shell commands \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mPart 2 is committed (\u001b[38;2;177;185;249m8625139\u001b[39m). Next is part 3, a behaviour-tree task\u001b[72Ganswered\u001b[81Gby\u001b[84Ga\u001b[86Gscript.\u001b[94GI'm\u001b[98Greading\u001b[106Ghow\u001b[110Gan\u001b[113Ginput\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcall\u001b[8Gis\u001b[11Gmade,\u001b[17Gso\u001b[20Gthe\u001b[24Gtask\u001b[29Gcall\u001b[34Gcan\u001b[38Gfollow\u001b[45Gthe\u001b[49Gsame\u001b[54Gpath.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[3G\u001b[39mReading\u001b[11G\u001b[1m1\u001b[22m file…\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;228;144;112mSimmering…\r\u001b[18C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m(shift+tab to cycle) · esc to inte\u001b[54Grupt · ← 1 agent\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
