[0.940, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdd\u001b[10Gd \u001b[1m3\u001b[22m lines,\u001b[21Gremoved\u001b[29G\u001b[1m1\u001b[31G\u001b[22mline\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 58 \u001b[11G\u001b[22mFrom\u001b[16Gthe\u001b[20Gsame\u001b[25Glayouts\u001b[33Gthe\u001b[37Ghost\u001b[42Gwrites\u001b[49Gthe\u001b[53Gbindings\u001b[62Ga\u001b[64Gscript\u001b[71Gis\u001b[74Gcompiled\u001b[83Gagainst,\u001b[92Ga\u001b[94GC\u001b[96Gheader\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[2m 59 \u001b[22m (`jettison_script.h`) and a\u001b[39GRust\u001b[44Gmodule\u001b[51G(`jettison_script.rs`),\u001b[75Geach\u001b[80Gasserting\u001b[90Gevery\u001b[96Gstruct's\u001b[105Gsize\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 60 \u001b[11G\u001b[22mand\u001b[15Gevery\u001b[21Gfield's\u001b[29Goffset,\u001b[37Gso\u001b[40Ga\u001b[42Gscript\u001b[49Gbuilt\u001b[55Gagainst\u001b[63Ganother\u001b[71Gbuild's\u001b[79Gtypes\u001b[85Gfails\u001b[91Gto\u001b[94Gcompile\u001b[102Grather\r\u001b[1B \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 61 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthan misread memory.                                                                                   \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 61 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mthan misread memory. In Rust a string, an array and a struct that holds either carry the lifetime      \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 62 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mof the memory they point into, `'a`, with their pointer and count private: made from a `&str` or a     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 63 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mslice, or from a raw pointer only in `unsafe` (`jettison_string::from_raw`).                           \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 64 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 65 \u001b[22m Every point\u001b[23Gr and cou\u001b[33Gt a script hand\u001b[49G back\u001b[55Gis\u001b[58Gchecked\